":\\\"Animal Names from Movies \\u0026 TV Shows: 200+ Iconic Screen-Inspired Pet Names\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discover the best animal names from movies and TV shows. From Star Wars to Disney classics, find iconic screen-inspired pet names that bring cinematic magic to your companion.\\\",\\\"datePublished\\\":\\\"2026-06-19\\\",\\\"dateModified\\\":\\\"2026-07-06\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/about/\\\"},\\\"publisher\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"BestAnimalNames\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com\\\"},\\\"mainEntityOfPage\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"WebPage\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/animal-names-from-movies-tv-shows/\\\"},\\\"wordCount\\\":999,\\\"articleBody\\\":\\\"📋 Table of Contents  Why Screen-Inspired Names Are So Popular Naming your pet after a beloved movie or TV character is one of the most personal and joyful naming choices you can make. These names carry emotional weight — they connect your companion to stories that have moved you, made you laugh, or shaped your worldview. Every time you call 'Frodo' across the dog park or 'Leia' from the kitchen, you are not just summoning your pet — you are summoning the feelings those characters evoke. Screen-inspired names also serve as social signals. A dog named 'Gandalf' at the dog park announces your love for Lord of the Rings. A cat named 'Ripley' tells visitors you appreciate strong female protagonists. These names are cultural shorthand — they communicate something about who you are and what you love, creating instant connections with fellow fans. At BestAnimalNames.com, we've curated names from across the cinematic universe — from Disney classics to modern streaming hits — that work beautifully as pet names regardless of whether the person meeting your pet gets the reference. These names sound great on their own; the cultural connection is a bonus. Disney \\u0026 Pixar Pet Names Disney and Pixar have created some of the most beloved characters in film history — and many of their names are perfect for pets: \\u003cstrong\\u003eSimba\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The Lion King. Brave leadership. \\u003cstrong\\u003eNala\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Also Lion King. Loyal and fierce. \\u003cstrong\\u003eMufasa\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Wise and powerful. \\u003cstrong\\u003eBelle\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Beauty and the Beast. Bookish beauty. \\u003cstrong\\u003eBeast\\u003c/strong\\u003e — For large, gentle pets. \\u003cstrong\\u003eAriel\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The Little Mermaid. Curious and adventurous. \\u003cstrong\\u003eOlaf\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Frozen. Warm-hearted and funny. \\u003cstrong\\u003eElsa\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Frozen. Elegant and powerful. \\u003cstrong\\u003eMoana\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Brave and determined. \\u003cstrong\\u003eMaui\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Boisterous and lovable. \\u003cstrong\\u003eBuzz\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Toy Story. Confident and loyal. \\u003cstrong\\u003eWoody\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Also Toy Story. Classic and dependable. \\u003cstrong\\u003eRemy\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Ratatouille. Small but talented. \\u003cstrong\\u003eDory\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Finding Nemo. Forgetful but endearing. \\u003cstrong\\u003eNemo\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Finding Nemo. Determined little adventurer. \\u003cstrong\\u003eStitch\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Lilo \\u0026 Stitch. Mischievous and lovable. \\u003cstrong\\u003eMerida\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Brave. Independent and spirited. \\u003cstrong\\u003ePascal\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The loyal chameleon from Tangled. Star Wars Universe Pet Names Star Wars offers some of the most distinctive and powerful names in cinema. Perfect for pets with galactic-sized personalities: \\u003cstrong\\u003eLuke\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The hero's journey. Classic and aspirational. \\u003cstrong\\u003eLeia\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Strong, regal, and rebellious. \\u003cstrong\\u003eHan\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Charming rogue. \\u003cstrong\\u003eChewie\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Loyal, furry, and vocal — perfect for fluffy dogs. \\u003cstrong\\u003eYoda\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Small, wise, and powerful — ideal for small breeds. \\u003cstrong\\u003eObi-Wan\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Wise mentor (Obi for short). \\u003cstrong\\u003eAnakin\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Passionate and powerful. \\u003cstrong\\u003eRey\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Resilient and determined. \\u003cstrong\\u003eFinn\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Brave and good-hearted. \\u003cstrong\\u003ePoe\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Dashing and skilled. \\u003cstrong\\u003eKylo\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Intense and complex. \\u003cstrong\\u003eVader\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Commanding presence — for pets with dark coats. \\u003cstrong\\u003eGrogu\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The Child (Baby Yoda). Adorable and mysterious. \\u003cstrong\\u003eMando\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Strong and protective. \\u003cstrong\\u003eAhsoka\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Wise and agile. \\u003cstrong\\u003eJyn\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Fierce and determined. \\u003cstrong\\u003eCassian\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Steadfast and resourceful. \\u003cstrong\\u003eBB-8\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Round, rolling, and lovable. Marvel Cinematic Universe Names The MCU has given us heroes, villains, and sidekicks whose names carry power, humor, and heart: \\u003cstrong\\u003eTony\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Iron Man. Charming and brilliant. \\u003cstrong\\u003ePepper\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Steadfast and capable. \\u003cstrong\\u003eThor\\u003c/strong\\u003e — God of Thunder — for powerful, noble pets. \\u003cstrong\\u003eLoki\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Mischievous and clever. \\u003cstrong\\u003eNatasha\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Black Widow. Fierce and loyal. \\u003cstrong\\u003eSteve\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Captain America. Noble and true. \\u003cstrong\\u003eBucky\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Loyal protector. \\u003cstrong\\u003ePeter\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Spider-Man. Young and enthusiastic. \\u003cstrong\\u003eGroot\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Says only one thing, means everything. \\u003cstrong\\u003eRocket\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Small, fierce, and brilliant. \\u003cstrong\\u003eGamora\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Deadly and loyal. \\u003cstrong\\u003eShuri\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Genius and lively. \\u003cstrong\\u003eT'Challa\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Majestic and wise. \\u003cstrong\\u003eCarol\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Captain Marvel. Powerful and fearless. \\u003cstrong\\u003eWanda\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Deeply feeling and powerful. \\u003cstrong\\u003eVision\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Thoughtful and unique. \\u003cstrong\\u003eHawkeye\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Sharp and dependable (Hawk for short). \\u003cstrong\\u003eFury\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Commanding and mysterious. Fantasy TV Series Names Epic fantasy series have created some of the most memorable character names that translate beautifully to pets: \\u003cstrong\\u003eGame of Thrones:\\u003c/strong\\u003e Arya (fierce and determined), Sansa (graceful and resilient), Tyrion (clever and underestimated), Brienne (noble and strong), Ghost (the direwolf — perfect for white pets), Nymeria (independent and protective), Drogon (powerful dragon), Rhaegal (noble dragon), Viserion (golden dragon). \\u003cstrong\\u003eLord of the Rings:\\u003c/strong\\u003e Frodo (brave and determined), Samwise (loyal beyond measure — perfect for dogs), Gandalf (wise and powerful), Aragorn (noble leader), Legolas (swift and graceful), Gimli (stout and fierce), Arwen (elven beauty), Eowyn (shieldmaiden — strong and brave), Pippin (curious and mischievous), Merry (loyal and clever). \\u003cstrong\\u003eThe Witcher:\\u003c/strong\\u003e Geralt (stoic and skilled), Yennefer (powerful and complex), Ciri (destined and fierce), Jaskier (charming and witty), Roach (Geralt's horse — a humble, loyal name). Classic Film Pet Names Some film characters are so iconic they have become timeless pet names across generations: \\u003cstrong\\u003eRocky\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The underdog who fights. \\u003cstrong\\u003eApollo\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Also Rocky. Confident and powerful. \\u003cstrong\\u003eIndy\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Indiana Jones. Adventurous. \\u003cstrong\\u003eMaverick\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Top Gun. Bold and independent. \\u003cstrong\\u003eGoose\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Loyal wingman. \\u003cstrong\\u003eRipley\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Alien. Survivor and protector. \\u003cstrong\\u003eNeo\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The Matrix. The One. \\u003cstrong\\u003eMorpheus\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Wise guide. \\u003cstrong\\u003eTrinity\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Powerful and sleek. \\u003cstrong\\u003eForrest\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Forrest Gump. Pure-hearted. \\u003cstrong\\u003eHolly\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Breakfast at Tiffany's. Chic and iconic. \\u003cstrong\\u003eFerris\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Ferris Bueller. Charming and clever. \\u003cstrong\\u003eMarty\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Back to the Future. Adventurous. \\u003cstrong\\u003eDoc\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Also Back to the Future. Eccentric genius. \\u003cstrong\\u003eInigo\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The Princess Bride. Skilled and driven. \\u003cstrong\\u003eButtercup\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Also Princess Bride. Beloved. Animated Film Names Beyond Disney Non-Disney animation has produced its own roster of memorable characters: \\u003cstrong\\u003eShrek\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Grumpy exterior, heart of gold — for bulldogs or gruff-looking pets. \\u003cstrong\\u003eFiona\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Strong and loving. \\u003cstrong\\u003eDonkey\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Chatty and loyal. \\u003cstrong\\u003eHiccup\\u003c/strong\\u003e — How to Train Your Dragon. Underestimated and brilliant. \\u003cstrong\\u003eToothless\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Also HTTYD. Fierce but gentle. \\u003cstrong\\u003ePo\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Kung Fu Panda. Enthusiastic and surprising. \\u003cstrong\\u003eTigress\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Also Kung Fu Panda. Disciplined and powerful. \\u003cstrong\\u003eKubo\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Kubo and the Two Strings. Creative and brave. \\u003cstrong\\u003eCoraline\\u003c/strong\\u003e — Curious and courageous. \\u003cstrong\\u003eKorra\\u003c/strong\\u003e — The Legend of Korra. Strong-willed and determined. Explore our name generators for {aardwolf}, {anthias}, {american-kestrel}, {andean-fox}, and {amur-leopard} to find the perfect name for your companion. Frequently Asked Questions Discover more naming ideas: {eagle}, {watchman-goby}, {orca}, {russian-tortoise}, {chausie}, and hundreds more animal name generators.\\\",\\\"image\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/images/og/blog-animal-names-from-movies-tv-shows.png\\\",\\\"inLanguage\\\":\\\"en\\\"}\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"14:[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"script\\\",null,{\\\"type\\\":\\\"application/ld+json\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"$1d\\\"}}],\\\"$L1e\\\",\\\"$L1f\\\",\\\"$L20\\\",\\\"$L21\\\"]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"22:T62a,\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"FAQPage\\\",\\\"mainEntity\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Question\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Will my pet respond to a movie-inspired name?\\\",\\\"acceptedAnswer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Answer\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Absolutely. Pets respond to sound and tone, not cultural references. A name like 'Chewie' or 'Yoda' is phonetically clear and distinctive — perfect for pet recognition.\\\"}},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Question\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"What if the character's personality doesn't match my pet?\\\",\\\"acceptedAnswer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Answer\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"That is often part of the fun. A tiny Chihuahua named 'Thor' or a lazy cat named 'Rocket' creates delightful irony that makes people smile. Names don't have to be literal.\\\"}},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Question\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Are there copyright issues with movie-inspired pet names?\\\",\\\"acceptedAnswer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Answer\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"No. Naming your pet after a fictional character is personal use and perfectly legal. Only commercial use of character names (like selling branded pet products) requires licensing.\\\"}},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Question\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"What is the most popular movie-inspired dog name?\\\",\\\"acceptedAnswer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Answer\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Simba (The Lion King), Loki (Marvel), and Chewie (Star Wars) consistently rank among the most popular movie-inspired dog names across multiple surveys.\\\"}},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Question\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Should I use the full character name or a shortened version?\\\",\\\"acceptedAnswer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Answer\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Shorter versions often work better for daily use. 'Obi' instead of Obi-Wan, 'Drog' instead of Drogon, 'Rock' instead of Rocket. But full names are fine if they roll off your tongue easily.\\\"}}]}\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"script\\\",null,{\\\"type\\\":\\\"application/ld+json\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"$22\\\"}}]\\n1f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"script\\\",null,{\\\"type\\\":\\\"application/ld+json\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"@context\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://schema.org\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"@type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"itemListElement\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"@type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ListItem\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"position\\\\\\\":1,\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Home\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"@type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ListItem\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"position\\\\\\\":2,\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Blog\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"@type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ListItem\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"position\\\\\\\":3,\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Animal Names from Movies \\u0026 TV Shows: 200+ Iconic Screen-Inspired Pet Names\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://bestanimaln